<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady, oil mixed, meal down.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady, oil mixed, meal down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Central Indian soybean markets were closed to mark a Hindu feast on Thursday. Plant delivered soybean prices were steady. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were mixed. Soyoil solvent was up by 100 rupees per tonne on good demand from vanaspati manufacturers and soyoil refined was down by 200 rupees per tonne on increased selling from refineries.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices further decreased today on heavy selling against limited demand. Soymeal yellow was $312 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for exports. Rapeseed extraction was $111 per tonne FAS in bulk for export and was 3,950 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
